IMPORT prelude

-- Emergency Services Levy Act 2002 (Western Australia), read with Part 6A of the Fire and Emergency Services Act 1998 (WA)
-- -- the land owner: what emergency services levy is charged on my home, who must pay it, when, and what can follow if
-- it is not paid.
--
-- SEAT: the land owner -- the individual whose land is levied ("What emergency services levy is charged on my home?").
-- Every exported question is phrased as that owner would ask it. The Minister's determination, the local government's
-- assessment and the FES Commissioner's recovery powers are encoded only as what they mean for the owner.
--
-- THE SPLIT. The Emergency Services Levy Act 2002 has three sections. Only s 3 is operative: "The emergency services levy
-- determined under Part 6A of the Fire and Emergency Services Act 1998 is imposed." The Act fixes no rate, no amount, no
-- payer and no date: it exists so that the levy is imposed as a tax by an Act that does nothing else. Everything the
-- owner meets -- which land is levied, who is liable, how the amount is worked out, the notice, the due date, interest,
-- recovery, sale, objection -- is in Part 6A of the Fire and Emergency Services Act 1998 (the "FES Act"), which is
-- deposited as its own subject and is brought in here. The rates, minimum and maximum for each year are set by the
-- Minister's Gazette determination under FES Act ss 36G-36I, which is NOT deposited: they are INPUTS.
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED: ESL Act s 3 (imposition). FES Act: s 3 definitions of "leviable land", "levy", "levy year" and
-- "gross rental value" (borrowed from the Valuation of Land Act 1978: a FACT); s 3A ("owner", paragraphs (a)(i) and (d));
-- s 36B (levy payable on all land in an ESL category area); s 36D (exemptions by regulation: a FACT); s 36E (exemptions
-- in other enactments do not apply); s 36F(3) (a change of category cannot take effect in the year it is published);
-- s 36G(1)-(2) (the levy for the next year determined before 31 May or a declared day); s 36H(1), (3) (rate in the dollar
-- of gross rental value at 1 July; another basis); s 36I (minimum and maximum); s 36J(1), (3), (4) (assessment notice,
-- with the council rate notice; service on one joint owner); s 36L(1)(b) (assessment by the FES Commissioner); s 36M(2)
-- (due no earlier than 35 days after issue); s 36O (a charge on the land); s 36P (the owner liable; to whom payable;
-- joint and several); s 36Q (one payment unless instalments approved); s 36S(1), (5) (interest on unpaid levy);
-- s 36T(1)(a), (2) (apportionment between successive owners; reimbursement); s 36Z(1) (recovery from the owner on service
-- or a later owner); s 36ZC(1)-(2) (sale after 3 years unpaid, 6 months' notice); s 36ZD (caveat); s 36ZE (objection to
-- the purpose of use, 60 days); s 36ZF (review by the SAT); s 36ZH (objection does not stop liability; refund; 30 days).
--
-- Edition: compilation of the Emergency Services Levy Act 2002 (No. 39 of 2002) as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_24246.txt (legislation.wa.gov.au mrdoc 24246, retrieved 2026-09-07), compilation
-- table ending with the Fire and Emergency Services Legislation Amendment Act 2012 (No. 22 of 2012). Fire and Emergency
-- Services Act 1998 (No. 41 of 1998) as deposited at
-- ../../../fire-and-emergency-services-act-1998/registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_49451.txt (mrdoc 49451, retrieved
-- 2026-09-07). The annual Gazette determination of ESL categories, rates, minimum and maximum (indexed as
-- wa/emergency-services-levy-annual-determination, text not deposited) supplies INPUTS only.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the FES Act outside Part 6A; Division 1 (local government expenditure estimates, s 36A); s 36C (records);
-- the content of any exemption regulations (s 36D: a FACT) and partial exemptions; the Minister's method (s 36G(3)-(5));
-- amended valuations within the year (s 36H(2), the amended value is simply the value input); assessment of State and
-- local government land (ss 36L(1)(a), 36N); early-payment discounts, waivers and concessions (s 36R) and the Rates and
-- Charges (Rebates and Deferments) Act 1992 (pensioner and senior rebates and deferments: asked as a FACT where Part 6A
-- defers to it); interest rates (s 36S(2), Gazette); apportionment between owners of portions (s 36T(1)(b)); local
-- government accounts (ss 36U-36Y); court proceedings and costs (s 36Z(2), 36ZA); the conduct of a sale and the order of
-- proceeds (s 36ZC(3)-(5)); ESL agreements (Division 9); fees for emergency services (Part 6B) and volunteer firefighter
-- compensation; Crown land owners under s 3A(b)-(c) and mining and petroleum holders under s 3A(f).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill from the seat of the land owner, with the design defaults
-- ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as
-- advice. See NOTES.md.
--
-- Conventions. A levy year is a financial year (FES Act s 3: "levy year ... means the financial year for which the levy is
-- payable"), named by the calendar year in which it ENDS: 2029/30 is 2030. A day is written as the number YYYYMMDD.
-- Money is in dollars.

§ `Emergency Services Levy Act 2002 -- the land owner`

§§ `Arithmetic`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the greater of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT LEAST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

§§ `ESL Act s 3 -- the levy imposed`

-- ESL Act long title: "An Act to impose the emergency services levy determined under the Fire and Emergency Services Act
-- 1998." s 3: "The emergency services levy determined under Part 6A of the Fire and Emergency Services Act 1998 is
-- imposed." Nothing in the Act states a rate, an amount, a payer or a date.
@export Does the Emergency Services Levy Act itself fix how much levy I pay (s 3)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the Emergency Services Levy Act itself fix how much levy I pay` IS FALSE

§§ `FES Act ss 36B, 36D, 36E -- is my land leviable?`

-- s 36B: "Except as otherwise provided in this Part, the levy is payable each year to the FES Commissioner on all land that
-- is located in an ESL category area." s 3: "ESL category area means an area of Western Australia that is declared under
-- section 36F(2)" (by the Minister in the Gazette: a FACT). "leviable land means land on which the levy is payable".
-- s 36D: "The regulations may -- (a) provide for kinds of land that are exempt or partially exempt from the levy" (the
-- regulations are not deposited: whether the land is of an exempt kind is a FACT).
-- s 36E(1): an earlier enactment that "purports to exempt a person from liability to pay any rate, tax or imposition that
-- could be taken to include the levy does not exempt the person"; (2) nor does a later one exempting from "all rates,
-- taxes or impositions"; (3) "Subsection (2) does not apply to an enactment that expressly exempts a person from liability
-- to pay the levy."
DECLARE `My land for the levy year` HAS
    `is located in an ESL category area` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is of a kind wholly exempt from the levy under the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
    `another enactment purports to exempt me from it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `that enactment was passed after section 36E commenced` IS A BOOLEAN
    `that enactment expressly exempts me from the levy` IS A BOOLEAN

@export Does another law's exemption from rates or taxes free me from the levy (FES Act s 36E)?
GIVEN `the land` IS A `My land for the levy year` @desc Your land and any other law that claims to exempt you
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does another law exempt me from the levy` IF
        `the land`'s `another enactment purports to exempt me from it`
    AND `the land`'s `that enactment was passed after section 36E commenced`
    AND `the land`'s `that enactment expressly exempts me from the levy`

@export Is my land leviable land, on which the emergency services levy is charged (FES Act ss 3, 36B, 36D, 36E)?
GIVEN `the land` IS A `My land for the levy year` @desc Your land for the levy year
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my land leviable` IF
        `the land`'s `is located in an ESL category area`
    AND (NOT (`the land`'s `is of a kind wholly exempt from the levy under the regulations`))
    AND (NOT (`Does another law exempt me from the levy` `the land`))

§§ `FES Act ss 3A, 36P -- am I the one liable?`

-- s 3A: "owner ... (a) in relation to Crown land, means -- (i) a lessee of the land or another person with a right to
-- occupy the land ...; (d) in relation to freehold land that is under the operation of the Transfer of Land Act 1893, means
-- a proprietor within the meaning of that Act, except a mortgagee who is not a mortgagee in possession of the land".
-- A tenant of freehold land is not within any paragraph of s 3A (INFERENCE from the text: the tenant is not the
-- proprietor, and paragraph (a) is confined to Crown land).
DECLARE `My interest in the land` IS ONE OF
    `registered proprietor of freehold land`
    `mortgagee not in possession`
    `mortgagee in possession`
    `lessee or occupier of Crown land`
    `tenant of freehold land`

@export Am I an owner of the land for the levy (FES Act s 3A)?
GIVEN `my interest` IS A `My interest in the land` @desc What your interest in the land is
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I an owner of the land` IS
    CONSIDER `my interest`
    WHEN `registered proprietor of freehold land` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `mortgagee not in possession` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `mortgagee in possession` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `lessee or occupier of Crown land` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `tenant of freehold land` THEN FALSE

-- s 36P(1): "A person who is the owner of leviable land is liable to pay the levy for a levy year."
@export Am I liable to pay the emergency services levy on this land for the levy year (FES Act s 36P(1))?
GIVEN `my interest` IS A `My interest in the land` @desc What your interest in the land is
      `the land` IS A `My land for the levy year` @desc Your land for the levy year
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I liable to pay the levy` IF
    `Am I an owner of the land` `my interest` AND `Is my land leviable` `the land`

-- s 36P(3): "If leviable land is owned by 2 or more persons, they are jointly and severally liable to pay the levy."
@export Can I be made to pay all of the levy on land I own with others (FES Act s 36P(3))?
GIVEN `I own the land with others` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the land is owned by you and one or more others
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I be made to pay all of the levy on land I own with others` IF `I own the land with others`

§§ `FES Act ss 36G, 36H, 36I -- how much?`

-- s 36G(1): "Before the relevant day each year, the Minister, by notice published in the Gazette, is to determine the
-- emergency services levy that is payable for the next levy year". (2) "relevant day means -- (a) a day declared by the
-- Minister ...; or (b) if no day is declared under paragraph (a), 31 May."
@export By what day must the levy for this levy year be determined in the Gazette (FES Act s 36G)?
GIVEN `the levy year` IS A NUMBER @desc The levy year, named by the year in which it ends (2029/30 is 2030)
      `the Minister declared another day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Minister declared a relevant day other than 31 May
      `the declared day` IS A NUMBER @desc The declared day, as YYYYMMDD (ignored if none was declared)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `By what day must the levy for this year be determined` IS
    IF `the Minister declared another day`
    THEN `the declared day`
    ELSE (`the levy year` MINUS 1) TIMES 10000 PLUS 531

-- s 36H(1): "the levy payable for a levy year on land is to be determined as a rate in the dollar of the gross rental value
-- of the land in force under the Valuation of Land Act 1978 as at 1 July in the levy year."
@export On which day is the gross rental value fixed that my levy is worked out on (FES Act s 36H(1))?
GIVEN `the levy year` IS A NUMBER @desc The levy year, named by the year in which it ends (2029/30 is 2030)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `On which day is the gross rental value for my levy fixed` IS (`the levy year` MINUS 1) TIMES 10000 PLUS 701

-- The Minister's determination for the land's ESL category area and purpose of use (s 36G(4)). Not deposited: INPUTS.
-- s 36H(3): if "impracticable or otherwise inappropriate", the Minister may determine the levy "(a) as a rate in the
-- dollar of the gross rental value of a portion of the land; or (b) on any other basis". Answered conditionally.
-- s 36I(1): "Despite any other provision of this Part, the Minister may determine -- (a) the minimum amount of levy
-- payable on land; and (b) the maximum amount of levy payable on land."
DECLARE `The determination for my land` HAS
    `rate in the dollar of gross rental value` IS A NUMBER
    `a minimum is determined` IS A BOOLEAN
    `minimum levy` IS A NUMBER
    `a maximum is determined` IS A BOOLEAN
    `maximum levy` IS A NUMBER
    `the Minister determined the levy on my land on another basis` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the levy on that other basis` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the determination` IS A `The determination for my land`
      `the gross rental value` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the levy before the minimum and maximum` MEANS
    IF `the determination`'s `the Minister determined the levy on my land on another basis`
    THEN `the determination`'s `the levy on that other basis`
    ELSE `the determination`'s `rate in the dollar of gross rental value` TIMES `the gross rental value`

GIVEN `the determination` IS A `The determination for my land`
      `the amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`raised to the minimum` MEANS
    IF `the determination`'s `a minimum is determined`
    THEN `the greater of` `the amount` (`the determination`'s `minimum levy`)
    ELSE `the amount`

GIVEN `the determination` IS A `The determination for my land`
      `the amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`held to the maximum` MEANS
    IF `the determination`'s `a maximum is determined`
    THEN `the lesser of` `the amount` (`the determination`'s `maximum levy`)
    ELSE `the amount`

@export How much emergency services levy is charged on my land for the levy year (FES Act ss 36B, 36H, 36I)?
GIVEN `the land` IS A `My land for the levy year` @desc Your land for the levy year
      `the determination` IS A `The determination for my land` @desc The Minister's Gazette determination for your land's category and use
      `the gross rental value` IS A NUMBER @desc The gross rental value of the land in force at 1 July in the levy year
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much levy is charged on my land` IS
    IF `Is my land leviable` `the land`
    THEN `held to the maximum` `the determination`
            (`raised to the minimum` `the determination`
                (`the levy before the minimum and maximum` `the determination` `the gross rental value`))
    ELSE 0

-- s 36F(3): "A notice under subsection (2) cannot have effect in respect of the levy year in which the notice is
-- published." A notice declaring an area's category, or moving it to another category, first counts the next year.
@export Can a change to my area's ESL category affect my levy for this levy year (FES Act s 36F(3))?
GIVEN `the levy year the notice was published in` IS A NUMBER @desc The levy year in which the Gazette notice was published
      `the levy year` IS A NUMBER @desc The levy year you are asking about
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can a change to my area's category affect this year's levy` IF
    `the levy year` GREATER THAN `the levy year the notice was published in`

§§ `FES Act ss 36J, 36L, 36P(2) -- the notice, and whom I pay`

-- s 36J(1): the local government is to "(a) assess the amount of levy payable ... by each person who owns leviable land in
-- its local government district; and (b) serve written notice of the assessment on the person." (4) "The assessment
-- notice is to be given by a local government -- (a) as part of the rate notice given under section 6.41 of the Local
-- Government Act 1995; or (b) if no rate notice is to be given -- as a separate notice." s 36L(1)(b): the FES
-- Commissioner "may assess the amount of levy payable for a levy year on land owned by any other person".
DECLARE `Who assessed my levy` IS ONE OF
    `my local government`
    `the FES Commissioner`

DECLARE `How my levy notice comes` IS ONE OF
    `as part of my council rate notice`
    `as a separate notice from my local government`
    `as a notice from the FES Commissioner`

@export How will my emergency services levy assessment notice come to me (FES Act ss 36J(4), 36L)?
GIVEN `the assessor` IS A `Who assessed my levy` @desc Who assessed the levy on your land
      `my local government gives me a rate notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your council gives you a rate notice for the year
GIVETH A `How my levy notice comes`
DECIDE `How will my levy notice come to me` IS
    CONSIDER `the assessor`
    WHEN `my local government` THEN
        IF `my local government gives me a rate notice`
        THEN `as part of my council rate notice`
        ELSE `as a separate notice from my local government`
    WHEN `the FES Commissioner` THEN `as a notice from the FES Commissioner`

-- s 36P(2): "The levy is payable -- (a) if an assessment notice is served on the person by a local government under
-- section 36J(1) -- to the local government; or (b) if an assessment notice is served on the person by the FES
-- Commissioner under section 36L(2) -- to the FES Commissioner."
@export Do I pay my emergency services levy to my local government (FES Act s 36P(2))?
GIVEN `the assessor` IS A `Who assessed my levy` @desc Who served the assessment notice on you
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I pay my levy to my local government` IS
    CONSIDER `the assessor`
    WHEN `my local government` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the FES Commissioner` THEN FALSE

-- s 36J(3): "If leviable land is owned by 2 or more persons, service of the assessment notice on one of those persons is
-- taken to be service of the notice on each of them." (Applied to the FES Commissioner's notices by s 36L(3).)
@export Is a levy notice served on my co-owner taken to be served on me (FES Act s 36J(3))?
GIVEN `I own the land with others` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the land is owned by you and one or more others
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a notice served on my co-owner served on me` IF `I own the land with others`

§§ `FES Act ss 36M, 36Q, 36S -- when, how, and interest`

-- s 36M(1): "The levy becomes due and payable on the date determined by the Minister and stated in the assessment
-- notice"; (2) "The date ... must not be earlier than 35 days after the date stated in the assessment notice as the date
-- the assessment notice was issued."
@export At the earliest, how many days after my notice was issued can my levy fall due (FES Act s 36M(2))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many days after my notice was issued can my levy fall due at the earliest` IS 35

@export Can my levy fall due this many days after the date my notice was issued (FES Act s 36M(2))?
GIVEN `the days after issue` IS A NUMBER @desc Days from the issue date stated in the notice to the due date stated in it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my levy fall due this many days after issue` IF `the days after issue` AT LEAST 35

-- s 36Q: "(1) Subject to subsection (2), the levy is payable by a single payment. (2) The Minister may approve -- (a)
-- arrangements for the levy to be paid by instalments; and (b) the charges applicable". s 36R(2): a local government
-- "may accept payment ... in accordance with an agreement made between the local government and the person."
@export May I pay my levy other than in one payment (FES Act ss 36Q, 36R(2))?
GIVEN `the Minister has approved instalment arrangements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether instalment arrangements are approved for the levy
      `I have a payment agreement with my local government` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you made a payment agreement with the council
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I pay my levy other than in one payment` IF
    `the Minister has approved instalment arrangements` OR `I have a payment agreement with my local government`

-- s 36S(1): "interest accrues on the levy, or an instalment of the levy, that is not paid ... from the time it becomes due
-- and payable." (5) "No interest is to accrue on the levy ... payable by -- (a) a person entitled under the Rates and
-- Charges (Rebates and Deferments) Act 1992 to a rebate or deferment in respect of the levy; or (b) a person of a kind
-- prescribed by the regulations." The rate is declared in the Gazette (s 36S(2)): not encoded.
@export Does interest run on my unpaid levy (FES Act s 36S)?
GIVEN `it is unpaid after its due date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the levy or an instalment is unpaid after it fell due
      `I am entitled to a rebate or deferment of the levy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are entitled to a rebate or deferment under the Rates and Charges (Rebates and Deferments) Act 1992
      `I am of a kind prescribed as free of interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the regulations prescribe you as a person on whom no interest accrues
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does interest run on my unpaid levy` IF
        `it is unpaid after its due date`
    AND (NOT `I am entitled to a rebate or deferment of the levy`)
    AND (NOT `I am of a kind prescribed as free of interest`)

§§ `FES Act ss 36T, 36O, 36Z -- buying and selling`

-- s 36T(1): the levy "(a) is apportionable between successive owners of the land in respect of time as if the levy accrued
-- from day to day during the levy year". The day counts are FACTS.
@export What part of the year's levy is apportioned to me as a successive owner (FES Act s 36T(1)(a))?
GIVEN `the levy for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc The levy for the whole levy year
      `the days I owned the land` IS A NUMBER @desc Days of the levy year for which you owned the land
      `the days in the levy year` IS A NUMBER @desc Days in the levy year (365, or 366)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What part of the year's levy is apportioned to me` IS
    `the levy for the year` TIMES `the days I owned the land` DIVIDED BY `the days in the levy year`

-- s 36T(2): "If any part of the levy payable on any land has been paid by a person other than the owner of the land ...
-- the owner is liable, if there is no agreement between them to the contrary, to reimburse that person the amount paid."
-- (3) "This section does not affect the liability of a person to pay the levy to a local government or to the FES
-- Commissioner."
@export Must I reimburse someone else who paid levy on my land (FES Act s 36T(2))?
GIVEN `someone other than me paid levy on my land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether another person paid part of the levy on land you own
      `we agreed otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and that person agreed that you need not reimburse
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I reimburse someone who paid levy on my land` IF
    `someone other than me paid levy on my land` AND (NOT `we agreed otherwise`)

-- s 36O: "Subject to the Rates and Charges (Rebates and Deferments) Act 1992, the levy, together with any costs of
-- proceedings for the recovery of the levy and any levy interest, is a charge on the leviable land."
-- s 36Z(1): the levy "is recoverable by the local government ... or by the FES Commissioner from -- (a) the owner of the
-- land on the date the assessment notice was served; or (b) a person who becomes the owner of the land while the levy is
-- unpaid."
@export Can levy left unpaid on this land be recovered from me (FES Act s 36Z(1))?
GIVEN `I owned the land when the notice was served` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were the owner on the day the assessment notice was served
      `I became the owner while the levy was unpaid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you became owner later, while that levy was still unpaid
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can unpaid levy on this land be recovered from me` IF
    `I owned the land when the notice was served` OR `I became the owner while the levy was unpaid`

-- s 36O is "subject to" the Rates and Charges (Rebates and Deferments) Act 1992; what that Act does to a rebated or
-- deferred amount is not encoded.
@export Is unpaid levy, with interest and recovery costs, a charge on my land (FES Act s 36O)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is unpaid levy a charge on my land` IS TRUE

§§ `FES Act ss 36ZC, 36ZD -- what can happen to my land if I do not pay`

-- s 36ZC(1): "If an amount of levy that is due and payable on any land has been unpaid for 3 years or more, the FES
-- Commissioner may apply to the Supreme Court for an order for the sale of the land". (2) "At least 6 months before ...
-- the FES Commissioner is to -- (a) have notice of the intended application published in 2 newspapers ...; (b) if the
-- whereabouts of the owner of the land is known ... give written notice of the intended application to that person".
-- The sale itself is for the Court (s 36ZC(3)): answered as whether the application may be made.
@export Can an application be made to sell my land for unpaid levy (FES Act s 36ZC(1)-(2))?
GIVEN `the years the levy has been unpaid` IS A NUMBER @desc Whole years the levy has been due and unpaid
      `the months since notice of the intended application` IS A NUMBER @desc Months since the newspaper notices (and your notice, if your whereabouts are known) were given
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can an application be made to sell my land` IF
    `the years the levy has been unpaid` AT LEAST 3 AND `the months since notice of the intended application` AT LEAST 6

-- s 36ZD: "If the levy that is due and payable on any land is unpaid, the Minister has an interest in the land in respect
-- of which the FES Commissioner may lodge a caveat to preclude dealings in relation to the land".
@export Can a caveat be lodged against my land for unpaid levy (FES Act s 36ZD)?
GIVEN `levy due on my land is unpaid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether levy that has fallen due on your land is unpaid
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can a caveat be lodged against my land` IF `levy due on my land is unpaid`

§§ `FES Act ss 36ZE, 36ZF, 36ZH -- objecting`

-- s 36ZE(1): "If section 36G(4)(b) or 36I(2)(b) applies to the determination of the levy payable on any land [different
-- rates or amounts by purpose of use], the owner of the land may object to the determination under section 36G(5) of the
-- purpose for which the land is used." (2) the objection is to be "(a) in writing ... (d) served on the Minister within 60
-- days after the date the assessment notice was served." (3) The Minister may extend the time "whether or not the time
-- for doing so has expired" (a judgment of the Minister: answered conditionally).
@export May I object to the purpose for which my land is taken to be used (FES Act s 36ZE(1))?
GIVEN `my levy depends on the purpose of use` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the rate or the minimum or maximum for your land differs by the purpose it is used for
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I object to the purpose my land is taken to be used for` IF `my levy depends on the purpose of use`

@export Is my objection in time (FES Act s 36ZE(2)(d), (3))?
GIVEN `the days after my notice was served` IS A NUMBER @desc Days from service of the assessment notice to service of your objection on the Minister
      `the Minister extended the time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Minister, on your application, extended the time far enough
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my objection in time` IF
    `the days after my notice was served` AT MOST 60 OR `the Minister extended the time`

-- s 36ZF: "A person who is dissatisfied with the determination of the Minister on an objection by the person under
-- section 36ZE may apply to the State Administrative Tribunal for a review".
@export May I apply to the State Administrative Tribunal for review (FES Act s 36ZF)?
GIVEN `I objected and the Minister has determined my objection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you objected under s 36ZE and the Minister decided it
      `I am dissatisfied with the determination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are dissatisfied with the Minister's decision
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I apply to the State Administrative Tribunal` IF
    `I objected and the Minister has determined my objection` AND `I am dissatisfied with the determination`

-- s 36ZH(1): "Pending determination of the objection, the liability to pay the levy on any land is not affected by -- (a)
-- an objection to the valuation of the land under the Valuation of Land Act 1978; or (b) an objection under this
-- Division."
@export Must I still pay the levy while my objection is pending (FES Act s 36ZH(1))?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I still pay the levy while my objection is pending` IS TRUE

-- s 36ZH(3): "(a) an amount by which, because of its adjustment, the levy was overpaid is to be refunded; and (b) an
-- amount by which ... the levy was underpaid is recoverable under section 36Z, but no action to recover that amount is to
-- be taken until at least 30 days after the notice ... is given". Interest on either is prescribed (not encoded).
@export How much is refunded to me when my levy is adjusted down (FES Act s 36ZH(3)(a))?
GIVEN `what I paid` IS A NUMBER @desc The levy you paid
      `the adjusted levy` IS A NUMBER @desc The levy as adjusted after the objection or review
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much is refunded to me after an adjustment` IS `the greater of` 0 (`what I paid` MINUS `the adjusted levy`)

@export For how many days after the adjustment notice am I safe from recovery of an underpayment (FES Act s 36ZH(3)(b))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many days after an adjustment notice before an underpayment can be pursued` IS 30
